    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nI setup mini.diff with latest save source, and if I have an empty line at the end of any of my files, then that line would be shown as Changed even though I don't make any modifications to the file. If I have multiple empty lines at the end then only the very last line has this issue.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In init.lua:\r\n```\r\nlocal MiniDiff = require('mini.diff')\r\nMiniDiff.setup({\r\n  view = {\r\n    style = 'sign'\r\n  },\r\n  source = MiniDiff.gen_source.save()\r\n})\r\n```\r\n2. Open any file with some text, go to the end of file, add 1 or a few empty lines, then save (:w).\r\n3. Should see the very last line shown as Changed\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe last empty line should not be marked as changed if it was not added since last saved.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c726dd00-ac05-48a3-8643-6f09271019ee)\r\n",
